{"seq":18,"at":"2026-11-06T11:40:39.280Z","type":"report.text","job":"A","data":{"step":"model-1","provider":"model-premium","text":"This report compares three ways regional grocers can reduce cold-chain spoilage: continuous temperature monitoring, refrigeration and transport upgrades, and tighter handling and inventory practices. The choice matters because perishables carry thin margins, so every discarded case erodes profit. Regional operators also have less capital and fewer backup systems than national chains. The goal is to show which approach fits a given store's budget, climate, and the patterns in its own shrink records."},"prev":"9a8b571ced91d5c613aebe5f3394609898c6037f95114d99a48565b938f24941","hash":"8205c227f10cb1142d352c61dde76af13d7e56f8229d685095c1583d775a0a7d"}
